{"title":"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(non-rigorous)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (non-rigorous)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Function\" title=\"Function\">function</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is defined for all real numbers and satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/a/1ea76d26fe0b4be2d33ea4a9aab120cabc2d66a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2+x)=f(2-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/a/faa40ac3ece33d925e19d671ecc7153e8683f3ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(7+x)=f(7-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is a root for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/c/a8c9cbf3e3c04dc46dea71f60acd0cb704eabc4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />, what is the least number of roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/c/a8c9cbf3e3c04dc46dea71f60acd0cb704eabc4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> must have in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3dfb4f87c58a0a686d321de5d4059f5598e371c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1000\\leq x \\leq 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"145\" height=\"15\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/a/1ea76d26fe0b4be2d33ea4a9aab120cabc2d66a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2+x)=f(2-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />, then substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c01cb5b30f62778e5ce16693b5afb5b0d51edf70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=2+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/5/c456c408f9bdad6512fcb9b0834acbe22d483d0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(t)=f(4-t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5ba6292616bce7e60b16db61c7ea8bed80b33ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(t)=f(14-t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />. In particular,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/0/d407ac602141db64b842ec20ad7b9638e39bfb9f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(t)=f(4-t)=f(14-(4-t))=f(t+10)\\]\" width=\"354\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is a root, all multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are roots, and anything congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/8/c383e8b36a4151f9ec532779095183e7d3ffc9a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\pmod{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" /> are also roots. To see that these may be the only integer roots, observe that the function\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/f/d1f6e47e1c7f4c6baa45e814fa7223f5adc22adb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x) = \\sin \\frac{\\pi x}{10}\\sin \\frac{\\pi (x-4)}{10}\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"39\" />\nsatisfies the conditions and has no other roots.\n</p><p>In the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/060e64f2446ba6bc49179f4227f41a1d118d6273.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1000\\leq x\\leq 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"145\" height=\"15\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/3/1038785e77cdf7734f6ee2f8fed6de2ab19acc15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$201$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> numbers that are congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add35a50744cf14b4c89853f0ebd0868fd6767cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\pmod{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" />, therefore the minimum number of roots is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/f/e5f8d9f87d727bc5ab4f4bc8af8fb20ea94d8174.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{401}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28non-rigorous.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(non-rigorous)\">Solution 2 (non-rigorous)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (non-rigorous)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We notice that the function has reflectional symmetry across both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f7f6230166a491e7a471a03829c792496576480.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=7$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. We also use the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is a root. This shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7d65cfa316d639c9267398009812f3eb45fea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a1f563320251baffd8c317c10f81a836df20c8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> are also roots. We then apply the reflection across the other axis to form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/8/308d71a33c1cd3cd8e28fad6c2f86a8ff4fb7a70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\pm 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> as roots. Continuing this shows that the roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad04f982a375be9265e4888dc69ebc33876a664a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\mod 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/c/1dcd62ee2d26185ffdd9d302882e8fcc5cd9f0d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\mod 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" />. There are 200 positive roots and 200 negative roots. 0 is also a root, and adding these gives a result of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/f/e5f8d9f87d727bc5ab4f4bc8af8fb20ea94d8174.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{401}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/e/6de1ed57c3dd05eda151d6e778bba997cdfe20b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QED \\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Solution by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:A1b2\" title=\"User:A1b2\">a1b2</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since this is a recursive problem, list out the functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/2/562a91083e33775cdf050ea94f9e84d78a9c071c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/8/e68c56082db3d4756941a61d1f4f08fe46114108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and figure out what they would be equivalent to. Then find the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> values for the functions that are equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/2/562a91083e33775cdf050ea94f9e84d78a9c071c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/8/e68c56082db3d4756941a61d1f4f08fe46114108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />. You will notice that it starts at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, then it goes to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51c80ea5862b45877f08d698a0c893bd2806a2fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec186fd1809357d1f530bee2334ceb59d405b4f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, etc... each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> has two possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> values. However, we are only counting the total number of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> values, so ignore the double counted values. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/4/b1448945895653e436a228ebb3caf43c9deae319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0, \\pm 5, \\pm 10, \\pm 15... \\pm 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"228\" height=\"16\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5bea32bab5cf07da05af9eea56b84e09ebbe2da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$400 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/f/e5f8d9f87d727bc5ab4f4bc8af8fb20ea94d8174.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{401}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be an arbitrary zero. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad073242f0f6ba959a1c1736513c02654252ec9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=2-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/555da78a339e781c4ae514751bfe7935d5e19a04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2-z$\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/6/0b641ce1661a2f28bbd09eb4f73ae811f33c889c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+x=4-z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"106\" height=\"13\" />. Repeat with other equation to find if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a zero then so are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/2/43279d521bd01f08c53fa66502d24dc7d6f02aa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4-z$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/2529b64787a26e1628e509dd4795c57bb726a13f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14-z$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Now note that applying either of these twice will return <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, so we must apply them in an alternating fashion for distinct roots. Doing so to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> returns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/7/d7701e9469f26e22c106341791344b28f3196443.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"31\" height=\"13\" />, respectively. A pattern will emerge of each path hitting a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> moves. Hence, we will reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/0/8d0ba17b812699b3489043d9d4caae5140d492bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> jumps in either direction. Including zero, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f6b6876b3e16a2286f59a01e14a9b1d10c4db94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot200+1=\\boxed{401}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:N828335\" title=\"User:N828335\">N828335</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME\" title=\"1984 AIME\">1984 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1984 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1984\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> 